This file provides the step of how to use this site supplied code base.

Development Environment
1. Windows 11 2025 Update (Version 25H2)
2. Visual Studio 2022
3. Obtain a "Device Token" from your node operator, this will self configure your development environment.

Steps
1. Download the supplied Fido Provider here https://github.com/Money-2021/VaultedObjects/blob/main/Fido.dll
   and the Support file here: https://github.com/Money-2021/PaymentClient/blob/main/Support
2. Great new Visual Studio Net8.0 MSTest (Microsoft's built-in framework)
3. Download the UnitTest cases as provided
4. Adapt the supplied code to your local MSTest environment. including configuration of your DeviceToken pathway.
5. Execute the supplied UnitTest cases to verify correct operation of the code functionality.

Suggested MSTest flow
1. UseCase_coin_balance()
2. UseCase_coin_local_pay_to_sin()
3. UseCase_coin_balance() for each Sin to verify payment flow between payment parties.

Notes
1. Typically a professional developer should allocate around 30 minutes to complete the first test case.
2. Visual Studio should automatically download or request the download of all required Net8.0 supporting libraries.

Enjoy the new world of Information Theoretic Secured Payments.
